# BST-1324: pnpm-lock.yaml must never be merged textually. A textual splice of
# two concurrent dependency PRs produced a syntactically-valid, semantically
# broken lockfile that took main fully red twice on 2026-08-16 (#2483, #2485):
# an importer entry said `catalog:` but kept a stale resolution from before the
# catalog moved. merge=binary forces a conflict instead, and the resolution is
# always the same: take either side, then run a real `pnpm install` (NOT
# --frozen-lockfile) and commit the regenerated file.
# scripts/verify-lockfile-catalog-conformance.mjs is the backstop that catches
# a bad lockfile however it was produced.
pnpm-lock.yaml merge=binary
